      "claim": "The Tarsk Highland Volunteers satisfy the customary international law definition of an \"organized armed group\" capable of being classified as a militia under Article 4A(2)(c).",
      "reasoning": "Customary IHL requires that a militia have a command structure, a degree of permanence, and the capacity to carry out sustained military operations. The militia’s written code, hierarchical command, and logistical support from the Union of Tarsk demonstrate these attributes, establishing it as an organized armed group for the purposes of the Geneva Convention.",
      "citations": []
    },
