      "claim": "The militia member’s carrying of his rifle openly while engaged in combat preserves his combatant status despite wearing civilian clothing.",
      "reasoning": "Article 4A(2)(c) also mandates that militia members carry arms openly during combat and during any military operation preparatory to combat. The facts state that the individual carried his rifle openly, satisfying this requirement. The absence of distinctive insignia does not negate combatant status when the other criteria are met.",
