    },
    {
      "claim": "Under Article 4A(2) of the Third Geneva Convention, a captured combatant is entitled to prisoner‑of‑war status, and Ardovia’s refusal to grant such status violates the Convention.",
      "reasoning": "Article 4A(2) expressly provides that persons who qualify as combatants under its sub‑paragraphs shall, upon capture, be treated as prisoners of war. Having established that the individual meets the combatant criteria, Ardovia is legally obligated to accord him POW protections. Failure to do so breaches the Convention’s mandatory provisions.",
